<title>UK: DIARY -- UK new share issues - Gallaher, Soco Intl.</title>
<headline>DIARY -- UK new share issues - Gallaher, Soco Intl.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British tobacco group Gallaher makes its stock market debut next week, with a 2.2 billion stg listing on May 30 following its demerger from American Brands Inc.</p>
<p>The issue price has not been disclosed but analysts believe it will be around 310p per share.</p>
<p>The company controls 30 per cent of the British tobacco market, with products such as Benson &amp; Hedges and Silk Cut cigarettes, Hamlet cigars, Condor pipe tobacco and Old Holborn hand-rolling tobacco.</p>
<p>Share dealings in oil and gas company Soco International Plc begin on May 29 following a placing at 260p per share.</p>
<p>Soco is being formed by combining the assets of U.S-based Snyder Oil and UK's Cairn Energy.</p>
<p>Snyder oil will own a 14 to 17 per cent stake in the company which will use the 39.3 million stg of new money raised to develop its portfolio of projects, particularly those in Mongolia.</p>
